  "review_notes": [
    "ἕνεκεν takes for … sake whole and heads on sake: rules 71 and 95 make it an improper preposition, whose complex English frame heads on the frame's lexical noun. Rule 78's for … sake precedent is carried entirely by proper prepositions and does not reach an adverb governing a case; a head on for remains the competing reading.",
